      {
        "id": "reporting-introduction",
        "title": "3. A claim and a report of that claim",
        "practiceTopic": "reporting-introduction",
        "body": [
          "Direct speech gives a speaker’s words as an utterance. Indirect statement embeds their claim under a reporting verb. λέγει ὅτι ἐπλήγη means “He says that he was struck”: the passive aorist belongs to the claim, not to the act of reporting. Identifying the report does not certify its truth.",
          "With ὅτι or ὡς, the embedded clause remains finite. An infinitive construction is also common after suitable verbs: φησὶ τὸν στρατηγὸν παίειν. Its expressed subject is accusative; the general, not the reporting speaker, strikes. We develop the governing-verb patterns and relative tense in Lesson 40."
        ],
