              "feedback": "Correct. An indefinite relative clause can use ἄν with a subjunctive: ὃς ἂν βοηθῇ, “whoever helps.” A general temporal clause uses combinations such as ὅταν (ὅτε + ἄν), “whenever,” and ἐπειδάν, “whenever/when.” The construction envisages any occasion or person meeting the description, rather than identifying one completed event."
            }
