              "correct": true,
              "feedback": "Correct. An absolute construction supplies a circumstance without being a normal argument of the main clause. Impersonal participles often form an accusative absolute: ἐξόν, “it being permitted”; δέον, “it being necessary”; δυνατόν/ἀδύνατον ὄν, “it being possible/impossible.” An infinitive can complete the expression."
