        "body": [
          "A report can change the person of pronouns while retaining the identity of their referents. Direct “I acknowledge gods” may become “Socrates says that he acknowledges gods.” If several men are present, English “he” may be less clear than a repeated name. Greek reflexives can point back to the reporting subject; ordinary pronouns require contextual resolution.",
          "Negation also has scope. οὐ λέγει ὅτι ἀδικεῖ denies that he makes the statement; λέγει ὅτι οὐκ ἀδικεῖ reports a denial of wrongdoing. οὔ φησιν ἀδικεῖν commonly has the latter sense through negative raising. Read the governing construction and the argument rather than moving οὐ mechanically."
