      {
        "id": "primary-nested-clauses",
        "title": "4. Subordinate clauses inside reports",
        "practiceTopic": "primary-nested-clauses",
        "body": [
          "A report may contain a purpose, condition, relative, or question. Bracket it before translating: λέγει ὅτι, ἐὰν οἱ νέοι μανθάνωσιν, βελτίους ἔσονται. The condition belongs to the reported claim, while the outer ὅτι introduces that claim. Its subjunctive is licensed by ἐάν, not by the outer verb λέγει.",
          "Build an annotation with four fields: speaker, governing verb, clause type, and time/aspect. Then produce a faithful connected translation. In a longer passage, follow repeated nouns and pronouns across paragraph boundaries. A fair report can be followed by criticism; do not rewrite a speaker’s position merely to make it easier to reject."
        ],
